  "description": "BUSKUX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C134 H163 Ho5 O21 S12,3(C3 H6 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.551-5.455 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.81-179.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho5(μ5-OH)(μ3-OH)4(L1)(L2)2(acac)2(CH3OH)2]·3acetone·2CH3OH; empirical C145H189Ho5O26S12. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
